uares. Compute a, b, and the predicted ŷ at x = 4.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/fit-simple-regression.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/fit-simple-regression","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/fit-simple-regression.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/fit-simple-regression.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/compute-gradient-2d","title":"Compute a 2D gradient","description":"f(x, y) = x² + 3xy + y². Compute ∇f at (1, 2). In which direction should you step to decrease f fastest, and what is the directional derivative in that direction?","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/compute-gradient-2d.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/compute-gradient-2d","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/compute-gradient-2d.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/compute-gradient-2d.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/independence-inclusion-exclusion","title":"Independence and inclusion-exclusion","description":"P(A)=0.4, P(B)=0.5, P(A∩B)=0.2. Are A and B independent? Compute P(A∪B). If they were mutually exclusive, what would P(A∪B) be instead?","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/independence-inclusion-exclusion.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/independence-inclusion-exclusion","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/independence-inclusion-exclusion.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/independence-inclusion-exclusion.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/normal-tail-probability","title":"Normal tail probability","description":"Latency is Normal(μ=100ms, σ=20ms). Approximate P(X > 140ms) using the z-score and a standard normal table (Φ(2) ≈ 0.977). What fraction is within 1σ of the mean?","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/normal-tail-probability.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/normal-tail-probability","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/normal-tail-probability.md","aliases":["/curriculu