ngineering.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-ux-interface-design","title":"Design exercise: UX & Interface Design","description":"User goals, information architecture, interaction states, feedback, accessibility, usability testing, and design systems. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: userGoal, interactionStates, accessibility. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-ux-interface-design.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-ux-interface-design","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-ux-interface-design.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-ux-interface-design.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-real-time-application-engineering","title":"Design exercise: Real-time Application Engineering","description":"WebSockets, server-sent events, presence, synchronization, ordering, reconnects, optimistic UI, and conflict handling. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: connectionLifecycle, ordering, reconciliation. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-real-time-application-engineering.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-real-time-application-engineering","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-real-time-application-engineering.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-real-time-application-engineering.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-interactive-2d-3d-systems","title":"Design exercise: 2D/3D Interactive Systems","description":"Scene graphs, render loops, input, animation, physics, GPU pipelines, asset loading, and performance budgets. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: sceneState, renderLoop, frameBudget. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-interactive-2d-3d-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-interactive-2d-3d-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-interactive-2d-3d-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-interactive-2d-3d-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-multimodal-models","title":"Design exercise: Multimodal Models","description":"Joint text, image, audio, and video representations, encoders, projectors, fusion, generation, and cross-modal evaluation. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: modalityEncoders, fusion, crossModalEval. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-multimodal-models.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-multimodal-models","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-multimodal-models.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-multimodal-models.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-vision-models","title":"Design exercise: Vision Models","description":"Classification, detection, segmentation, embeddings, vision transformers, data augmentation, and visual evaluation. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: taskDefinition, representation, visualEval. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-vision-models.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-vision-models","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-vision-models.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-vision-models.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-pose-motion-tracking","title":"Design exercise: Pose & Motion Tracking","description":"Landmarks, skeletons, optical flow, temporal smoothing, identity tracking, calibration, occlusion, and latency. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: landmarks, temporalTracking, occlusionHandling. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-pose-motion-tracking.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-pose-motion-tracking","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-pose-motion-tracking.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-pose-motion-tracking.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-voice-audio-systems","title":"Design exercise: Voice & Audio Systems","description":"Capture, codecs, streaming, speech recognition, synthesis, turn detection, noise handling, latency, and conversational UX. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: audioPipeline, turnDetection, latencyBudget. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-voice-audio-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-voice-audio-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-voice-audio-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-voice-audio-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-image-video-generation","title":"Design exercise: Image & Video Generation","description":"Diffusion and transformer generation, conditioning, latent spaces, control, consistency, safety, and media evaluation. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: conditioning, generationProcess, qualityEval. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-image-video-generation.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-image-video-generation","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-image-video-generation.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-image-video-generation.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-robotics-systems","title":"Design exercise: Robotics Systems","description":"Sensing, localization, mapping, planning, control, simulation, safety, real-time loops, and hardware interfaces. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: perception, planningControl, safety. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-robotics-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-robotics-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-robotics-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-robotics-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-spatial-interfaces","title":"Design exercise: Spatial Interfaces","description":"Coordinate systems, anchors, tracking, depth, occlusion, hand/eye input, world understanding, and spatial UI. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: coordinateSystem, tracking, spatialInteraction. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-spatial-interfaces.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-spatial-interfaces","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-spatial-interfaces.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-spatial-interfaces.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-human-computer-interaction","title":"Design exercise: Human-Computer Interaction","description":"Human perception, cognition, motor control, interaction techniques, accessibility, evaluation, and responsible design. Implement designOutline() returning non-empty values for: userContext, interactionTechnique, evaluation. Each value must name a concrete mechanism or decision.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-human-computer-interaction.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-human-computer-interaction","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-human-computer-interaction.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-human-computer-interaction.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/analyse-amortised-growth","title":"Amortised growth of a dynamic array","description":"Implement pushCount(n): build a dynamic array by pushing n items, doubling capacity when full (starting at capacity 1), and return the TOTAL number of element copies performed. This is the sum that makes push O(1) amortised — for n=8 the copies are 1+2+4 = 7.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/analyse-amortised-growth.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/analyse-amortised-growth","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/analyse-amortised-growth.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/analyse-amortised-growth.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/stable-sort-by-key","title":"Stable sort by one key","description":"Implement sortByScore(rows) returning rows ordered by descending numeric `score`, with the original relative order preserved for equal scores (a stable sort). Do not mutate the input.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/stable-sort-by-key.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/stable-sort-by-key","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/stable-sort-by-key.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/stable-sort-by-key.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/size-a-write-heavy-service","title":"Size a write-heavy service","description":"Implement size(dau, writesPerUserPerDay, bytesPerWrite, replicationFactor, peakMultiplier) returning { writesPerSecond, peakWritesPerSecond, storagePerDayGB, storagePerYearTB }. Use 86400 s/day and 365 d/yr. Storage counts replication. Use GB = 1e9 bytes and TB = 1e12 bytes (decimal, as capacity planning does). Round every value to the nearest integer.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/size-a-write-heavy-service.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/size-a-write-heavy-service","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/size-a-write-heavy-service.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/size-a-write-heavy-service.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/classify-requirements","title":"Split functional from non-functional","description":"Implement classify(requirements) returning { functional, nonFunctional } — two arrays preserving input order. A functional requirement states what the system DOES; a non-functional one states a quality or constraint it must hold (latency, availability, throughput, durability, consistency, cost, security posture).","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/classify-requirements.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/classify-requirements","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/classify-requirements.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/classify-requirements.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/range-sum-queries","title":"Answer range-sum queries in O(1)","description":"Implement makeRangeSum(nums) returning a function query(i, j) that gives the inclusive sum of nums[i..j] in O(1) per call. Build the prefix array once.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/range-sum-queries.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/range-sum-queries","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/range-sum-queries.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/range-sum-queries.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/next-greater-element","title":"Next greater element","description":"Implement nextGreater(nums) returning an array where result[i] is the next element to the right strictly greater than nums[i], or -1 if none. Must be O(n) — each index pushed and popped at most once.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/next-greater-element.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/next-greater-element","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/next-greater-element.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/next-greater-element.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/rolling-hash-search","title":"Rabin-Karp substring search","description":"Implement findAll(text, pattern) returning every start index where pattern occurs, using a rolling hash. You MUST verify a character-by-character match on every hash hit — a hash collision is not a match.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/rolling-hash-search.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/rolling-hash-search","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/rolling-hash-search.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/rolling-hash-search.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/kruskal-mst-weight","title":"Total weight of a minimum spanning tree","description":"Implement mstWeight(n, edges) where edges are [u, v, w] on nodes 0..n-1. Return the total weight of a minimum spanning tree, or -1 if the graph is not connected. Use Kruskal with union-find.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/kruskal-mst-weight.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/kruskal-mst-weight","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/kruskal-mst-weight.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/kruskal-mst-weight.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/detect-write-skew","title":"Detect write skew under snapshot isolation","description":"Two transactions each read the same snapshot and then write DIFFERENT rows based on what they read — snapshot isolation permits this, and the invariant breaks. Implement wouldSkew(t1, t2) where each transaction is { reads: string[], writes: string[] }. Return true when they are a write-skew risk: their read sets overlap, at least one transaction writes a row the OTHER read, and they write disjoint rows. Return false otherwise.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/detect-write-skew.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/detect-write-skew","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/detect-write-skew.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/detect-write-skew.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/pick-a-join-strategy","title":"Pick the join the planner should pick","description":"Implement chooseJoin({ leftRows, rightRows, leftSorted, rightSorted, hasIndexOnRight, memoryRows }) returning 'nested-loop', 'hash', or 'merge'. Rules: if both inputs are already sorted on the key, merge. Otherwise if the smaller side exceeds memoryRows, fall back to merge (hash would spill). Otherwise if the right side has an index and the left is small (<= 100 rows), nested-loop. Otherwise hash.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/pick-a-join-strategy.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/pick-a-join-strategy","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/pick-a-join-strategy.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/pick-a-join-strategy.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/backoff-with-jitter","title":"Exponential backoff with full jitter","description":"Implement backoffDelays(attempts, baseMs, capMs, rand) returning the delay for each attempt using capped exponential backoff with FULL jitter: delay = rand() * min(capMs, baseMs * 2^attempt), floored to an integer. `rand` is a supplied function returning [0,1) so the result is deterministic under test. Attempt numbering starts at 0.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/backoff-with-jitter.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/backoff-with-jitter","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/backoff-with-jitter.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/backoff-with-jitter.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/parameterise-a-query","title":"Parameterise instead of escaping","description":"Implement buildQuery(table, filters) returning { text, values }: a parameterised SQL string using $1, $2 … placeholders in order, plus the values array. Column names come from a fixed ALLOWED set — reject anything else by throwing. Never interpolate a value into the string.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/parameterise-a-query.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/parameterise-a-query","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/parameterise-a-query.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/parameterise-a-query.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/utilisation-latency-curve","title":"Latency against utilisation","description":"For an M/M/1 queue implement mm1(lambdaRate, muRate) returning { rho, avgInSystem, avgWaitSeconds } where rho = λ/µ, L = ρ/(1−ρ), W = 1/(µ−λ). Return null when the queue is unstable (λ >= µ). Round rho to 2 decimals, avgInSystem to 2, avgWaitSeconds to 4.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/utilisation-latency-curve.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/utilisation-latency-curve","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/utilisation-latency-curve.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/utilisation-latency-curve.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/distance-concentration","title":"Distances concentrate as dimensions grow","description":"Implement contrast(points, query) returning (maxDist - minDist) / minDist using Euclidean distance — the relative contrast between the farthest and nearest point. Round to 3 decimals. Return 0 when minDist is 0.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/distance-concentration.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/distance-concentration","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/distance-concentration.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/distance-concentration.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/wand-threshold-skip","title":"Skip documents that cannot reach the top k","description":"Implement prune(docs, upperBounds, k) where docs is [{id, terms:[termName], score}] and upperBounds maps term -> max possible contribution. Walk docs in order maintaining a top-k heap; BEFORE scoring a document, skip it when the sum of its terms' upper bounds is <= the current k-th best score. Return { top: ids of the top k by score descending, scored: how many documents you actually scored }.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/wand-threshold-skip.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/wand-threshold-skip","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/wand-threshold-skip.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/wand-threshold-skip.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/token-bucket-limiter","title":"Token bucket rate limiter","description":"Implement makeLimiter(capacity, refillPerSecond) returning allow(nowMs) -> boolean. Tokens refill continuously at refillPerSecond, capped at capacity; the bucket starts full. Each allowed call consumes one token. Do not refill in discrete ticks.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/token-bucket-limiter.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/token-bucket-limiter","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/token-bucket-limiter.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/token-bucket-limiter.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/snowflake-id-layout","title":"Pack and unpack a Snowflake id","description":"Implement pack(timestampMs, machineId, sequence) and unpack(id) for a 64-bit Snowflake layout: 41 bits timestamp (ms since a custom epoch), 10 bits machine id, 12 bits sequence. Use BigInt. pack must throw when machineId or sequence exceeds its field.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/snowflake-id-layout.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/snowflake-id-layout","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/snowflake-id-layout.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/snowflake-id-layout.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/recurrence-depth","title":"Solve a divide-and-conquer recurrence","description":"Implement masterCase(a, b, fExp) for T(n) = a*T(n/b) + n^fExp. Let c = log_b(a). Return 'leaves' when fExp < c (leaf work dominates, T = n^c), 'balanced' when fExp === c (T = n^c log n), 'root' when fExp > c. Compare with a small tolerance — log_b(a) is floating point.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/recurrence-depth.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/recurrence-depth","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/recurrence-depth.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/recurrence-depth.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/kth-smallest-quickselect","title":"k-th smallest by quickselect","description":"Implement kthSmallest(nums, k) returning the k-th smallest (k is 1-based) using quickselect — partition, then recurse into only ONE side. Do not sort the array and do not mutate the caller's input.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/kth-smallest-quickselect.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/kth-smallest-quickselect","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/kth-smallest-quickselect.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/kth-smallest-quickselect.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/find-the-anomaly","title":"Spot the update anomaly","description":"Implement violatesThirdNF(columns, key, dependencies) -> boolean. `dependencies` is [{determinant: string[], dependent: string}]. Report a 3NF violation when a dependency's determinant is NOT a superset of the key AND its dependent is not itself part of the key — i.e. a non-key attribute determined by something other than the whole key.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/find-the-anomaly.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/find-the-anomaly","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/find-the-anomaly.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/find-the-anomaly.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/lru-k-eviction","title":"Why LRU-K survives a scan","description":"Implement simulate(capacity, accesses, policy) returning the number of hits. policy is 'lru' or 'lru2'. Under 'lru2' a page is only promoted into the resident set on its SECOND access — a page seen once goes to a probationary list and is evicted before any twice-seen page. Evict the least-recently-used within each tier, probationary first.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/lru-k-eviction.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/lru-k-eviction","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/lru-k-eviction.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/lru-k-eviction.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/keyset-pagination","title":"Cursor pagination that survives inserts","description":"Implement page(rows, cursor, limit) for keyset pagination. Rows are {id, createdAt} sorted by (createdAt, id) ascending. cursor is null for the first page or {createdAt, id} for 'resume strictly after this'. Return { items, nextCursor } where nextCursor is the last item's key, or null when the page is not full.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/keyset-pagination.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/keyset-pagination","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/keyset-pagination.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/keyset-pagination.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/count-with-inclusion-exclusion","title":"Count with inclusion-exclusion","description":"Implement countDivisible(n, divisors) — how many integers in 1..n are divisible by AT LEAST ONE of the divisors. Use inclusion-exclusion over every non-empty subset, adding odd-sized subsets and subtracting even-sized ones, with lcm for each subset.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/count-with-inclusion-exclusion.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/count-with-inclusion-exclusion","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/count-with-inclusion-exclusion.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/count-with-inclusion-exclusion.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/logsumexp-stable","title":"Log-sum-exp without overflow","description":"Implement logSumExp(xs) returning log(sum(exp(x))) that stays finite for large inputs by subtracting the maximum first. Must return a finite number for [1000, 1001, 1002], where the naive form overflows to Infinity.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/logsumexp-stable.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/logsumexp-stable","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/logsumexp-stable.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/logsumexp-stable.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/ndcg-at-k","title":"NDCG@k","description":"Implement ndcgAtK(relevances, k) where relevances are graded gains in RANKED order. DCG = sum over i of rel_i / log2(i + 2) for i from 0. IDCG uses the same relevances sorted descending. Return DCG/IDCG rounded to 4 decimals, or 0 when IDCG is 0.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/ndcg-at-k.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/ndcg-at-k","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/ndcg-at-k.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/ndcg-at-k.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/ipw-debias-clicks","title":"Debias clicks by inverse propensity","description":"Implement debiasedCtr(events, propensity) where events are {docId, position, clicked} and propensity maps position -> probability of examination. Return docId -> estimated relevance = (sum of clicks / propensity[position]) / (number of impressions). Round each value to 4 decimals.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/ipw-debias-clicks.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/ipw-debias-clicks","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/ipw-debias-clicks.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/ipw-debias-clicks.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/scalar-quantize-roundtrip","title":"Scalar quantise and rescore","description":"Implement quantize(vec, min, max) mapping each float to an int in 0..255, dequantize(codes, min, max) mapping back to the bucket centre, and maxAbsError(vec, min, max) returning the largest absolute reconstruction error. Values outside [min,max] clamp.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/scalar-quantize-roundtrip.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/scalar-quantize-roundtrip","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/scalar-quantize-roundtrip.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/scalar-quantize-roundtrip.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/count-random-reads","title":"Cost a disk-resident search by I/O","description":"Implement queryCost({hops, neighboursPerHop, cachedFraction, readLatencyUs, compareLatencyNs}) returning { randomReads, totalUs } rounded to 2 decimals. Every hop fetches neighboursPerHop nodes; a cachedFraction of them avoid the SSD. Comparisons cost compareLatencyNs each and happen for every fetched neighbour.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/count-random-reads.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/count-random-reads","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/count-random-reads.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/count-random-reads.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/tombstone-recall-drift","title":"Tombstones erode recall","description":"Implement search(graph, deleted, entry, query, k, budget) — a greedy walk over an adjacency map. Visit at most `budget` nodes; tombstoned nodes (in `deleted`) are traversed and count against the budget but must NOT appear in results. Return the ids of up to k live nodes with the smallest |value - query|, best first.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/tombstone-recall-drift.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/tombstone-recall-drift","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/tombstone-recall-drift.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/tombstone-recall-drift.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/cache-key-and-ttl","title":"Decide the edge cache key","description":"Implement edgePolicy({ url, hasAuthCookie, varyHeaders, contentHashed }) returning { cacheable, ttlSeconds, key }. Never cache when hasAuthCookie is true (ttl 0). A content-hashed URL is immutable: ttl 31536000. Otherwise ttl 300. The key is the url plus each varyHeader appended as '|<header>' in the given order.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/cache-key-and-ttl.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/cache-key-and-ttl","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/cache-key-and-ttl.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/cache-key-and-ttl.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-data-representation","title":"Encode a binary compatibility fixture","description":"Implement encodeRepresentations() without hard-coding the returned fixture. Return lowercase hexadecimal strings for four values: signed16Hex for -42 encoded as a 16-bit two's-complement integer, float32Hex for 0.15625 encoded as IEEE-754 binary32, utf8Hex for the string A€, and littleEndianHex for the 32-bit value 0x12345678 written little-endian.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-data-representation.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-data-representation","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-data-representation.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-data-representation.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/practice-program-memory-model","title":"Trace a program into process memory","description":"Implement memoryMap() for this C-shaped program: static int requests; int main() { char *buffer = malloc(4096); int count = 0; serve(buffer, &count); free(buffer); }. Return executable, stack, heap, pointer, and process strings. Each must be a distinct explanation of at least six words that names its storage, lifetime, ownership, or loading mechanism.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/practice-program-memory-model.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-program-memory-model","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/practice-program-memory-model.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/practice-program-memory-model.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/build-rules-first-workspace","title":"Build a scoped repository instruction map","description":"Implement instructionMap() for a repository with a root AGENTS.md and a packages/api/AGENTS.md. Return {root, api, precedence, checks}. root must contain exactly three concise repository-wide invariants. api must contain exactly two API-only refinements and must not repeat a root rule. precedence must explain in at least eight words that nearer instructions refine broader instructions without silently overriding direct task intent. checks must list two runnable validation commands.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/build-rules-first-workspace.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-rules-first-workspace","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-rules-first-workspace.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/build-rules-first-workspace.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/make-agent-readable-workspace","title":"Define an agent-readable environment contract","description":"Implement environmentContract(worktreeId) returning {bootstrap, readiness, workspace, capabilities}. bootstrap and readiness must each contain two runnable commands. workspace must include the supplied worktreeId and distinct port, database, and output identifiers derived from it. capabilities must explicitly list filesystem, network, and secrets as allow, deny, or scoped.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/make-agent-readable-workspace.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/make-agent-readable-workspace","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/make-agent-readable-workspace.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/make-agent-readable-workspace.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/build-multi-session-continuity","title":"Create a durable agent handoff","description":"Implement createHandoff(input) returning a JSON-safe object with schemaVersion 1, goal, status, completed, evidence, blockers, and nextAction. Reject an input that claims status 'complete' without evidence. nextAction must be one concrete action, not a list, and every evidence item must include both command and observed output.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/build-multi-session-continuity.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-multi-session-continuity","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-multi-session-continuity.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/build-multi-session-continuity.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/add-feedback-and-scope-control","title":"Enforce runtime scope and escalation","description":"Implement scopeDecision(contract, observation). contract contains allowedRoots, maxFiles, and objective. observation contains touchedFiles, objectiveSatisfied, and planInvalidated. Return 'continue' only while every file is inside an allowed root, file count is within budget, the objective is incomplete, and the plan remains valid. Return 'complete' only when the objective is satisfied within scope. Return 'escalate' for any scope breach or invalidated plan.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/add-feedback-and-scope-control.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/add-feedback-and-scope-control","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/add-feedback-and-scope-control.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/add-feedback-and-scope-control.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/separate-maker-and-checker","title":"Separate maker claims from checker evidence","description":"Implement checkerVerdict(contract, makerReport, observations). contract contains requiredChecks and maxChangedFiles. observations contains independently observed checks and changedFiles. Return {accepted, missing, reasons}. Acceptance must depend only on the contract and observations, never on makerReport.claimedPassed. A required check passes only when observations records it as 'passed'.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/separate-maker-and-checker.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/separate-maker-and-checker","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/separate-maker-and-checker.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/separate-maker-and-checker.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/build-complete-harness-lifecycle","title":"Implement a bounded agent run lifecycle","description":"Implement transitionRun(state, event). Valid states are queued, running, checking, complete, blocked, cancelled. start moves queued to running only when event.ready is true; submit moves running to checking; accept moves checking to complete only when event.evidenceCount is positive; reject moves checking back to running when budget remains and to blocked otherwise; cancel moves any non-terminal state to cancelled. Invalid transitions must throw.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/build-complete-harness-lifecycle.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-complete-harness-lifecycle","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/build-complete-harness-lifecycle.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/build-complete-harness-lifecycle.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/drills/evaluate-automated-agent-loop","title":"Evaluate and ablate an agent harness","description":"Implement compareHarness(baseline, candidate, limits). Each run has tasksPassed, tasksTotal, costUsd, minutes, interventions, and unsafeActions. Return successRateDelta, costDelta, timeDelta, and release. release is true only when candidate success rate does not regress, unsafeActions is zero, costUsd and minutes are within limits, and interventions do not exceed baseline.","assetPath":"/curriculum/drills/evaluate-automated-agent-loop.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/evaluate-automated-agent-loop","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/drills/evaluate-automated-agent-loop.md","aliases":["/curriculum/drills/evaluate-automated-agent-loop.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/search-ir","title":"Search & IR","description":"Lexical retrieval beyond embeddings: tokenization, inverted indexes, BM25, ranking, hybrid search, and search evaluation.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/search-ir.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/search-ir","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/search-ir.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/search-ir.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/mathematics","title":"Mathematics","description":"Active math only: solve, derive, implement, simulate — never aesthetic consumption. Stack: probability & statistics → linear algebra → optimization → quant bridge. No artifact, no learning.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/mathematics.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/mathematics","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/mathematics.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/mathematics.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/vector-db","title":"Vector DB & ANN","description":"Vector search engines: similarity, top-k, brute force, HNSW, IVF, quantization, metadata filtering, and recall/latency tradeoffs.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/vector-db.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/vector-db","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/vector-db.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/vector-db.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/ai-systems","title":"AI Systems","description":"Practical AI engineering: LLM apps, RAG, chunking, tool calling, agents, evals, and model/transformer foundations.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/ai-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/ai-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/ai-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/ai-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/backend","title":"Backend","description":"Production backend strength: HTTP, API design, auth, rate limiting, idempotency, queues, jobs, caching, and observability.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/backend.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/backend","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/backend.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/backend.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/databases","title":"Databases & Storage","description":"Storage foundations for Turbopuffer-class systems: B-trees, LSM trees, WAL, compaction, partitioning, replication, object storage.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/databases.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/databases","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/databases.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/databases.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/system-design","title":"System Design","description":"Architecture-level thinking: low-level design, scalability, distributed systems, event-driven design, and end-to-end case studies.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/system-design.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/system-design","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/system-design.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/system-design.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/dsa","title":"DSA & Implementation","description":"Fast, clean implementation ability: arrays, graphs, trees, dynamic programming, and the core algorithmic patterns.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/dsa.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/dsa","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/dsa.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/dsa.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/behavioral","title":"Behavioral & Communication","description":"The interview round that is not about code: influence, conflict, ownership, prioritisation, and learning from failure.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/behavioral.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/behavioral","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/behavioral.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/behavioral.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/go-to-market","title":"Go-to-Market","description":"Getting a built thing in front of people: positioning, landing pages, SEO, and product analytics.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/go-to-market.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/go-to-market","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/go-to-market.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/go-to-market.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/systems-foundations","title":"Systems Foundations","description":"Operating systems, networks, concurrency, hardware, runtimes, performance, security, and isolation.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/systems-foundations.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/systems-foundations","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/systems-foundations.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/systems-foundations.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/infrastructure-platforms","title":"Infrastructure & Platforms","description":"Cloud infrastructure, containers, CI/CD, orchestration, reliability, observability, sandboxes, and infrastructure automation.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/infrastructure-platforms.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/infrastructure-platforms","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/infrastructure-platforms.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/infrastructure-platforms.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/distributed-systems","title":"Distributed Systems","description":"Coordination, replication, partitioning, event systems, caching, durable workflows, consistency, and recovery.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/distributed-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/distributed-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/distributed-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/distributed-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/inference-serving","title":"Inference & Serving","description":"Inference engines, batching, KV caches, attention kernels, decoding, routing, hardware utilization, and serving economics.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/inference-serving.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/inference-serving","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/inference-serving.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/inference-serving.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/agent-systems","title":"Agent Systems","description":"Agent loops, tools, memory, MCP, coordination, durable execution, permissions, computer use, and long-running work.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/agent-systems.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/agent-systems","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/agent-systems.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/agent-systems.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/ai-reliability","title":"Evaluation & AI Reliability","description":"LLM and agent evaluations, regression gates, failure detection, tracing, verification, human review, and quality economics.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/ai-reliability.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/ai-reliability","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/ai-reliability.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/ai-reliability.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/developer-tools","title":"Developer Tools & Code Intelligence","description":"Code review, analysis, testing infrastructure, repository graphs, coding agents, supply-chain health, and remediation.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/developer-tools.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/developer-tools","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/developer-tools.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/developer-tools.md"]},{"path":"/curriculum/tracks/application-engineering","title":"Application Engineering","description":"Backend, web, mobile, product analytics, UX, real-time applications, interactive systems, and distribution loops.","assetPath":"/curriculum/tracks/application-engineering.md","url":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/application-engineering","md":"https://learn.significanthobbies.com/curriculum/tracks/application-engineering.md","aliases":["/curriculum/tracks/application-engineering.md"]